[>DESCRIPTION]
.B pyipmi
is the command line tool of the python\-ipmi library. It talks to IPMI
devices over the native RMCP and RMCP+ interfaces, the Linux IPMI and IPMB
drivers, an IPMB bus adapter or the
.BR ipmitool (1)
command as backend.
.PP
It is not
.BR ipmitool (1)
and does not accept the same options and commands.
.PP
The command was formerly called
.BR ipmitool.py ,
which is still installed as an alias.

[EXAMPLES]
Print the device ID of a BMC over RMCP+ (IPMI v2.0, like \fBipmitool \-I lanplus\fR):
.PP
.RS
pyipmi \-I rmcpplus \-H 10.0.0.1 \-U admin \-P admin bmc info
.RE
.PP
List the sensors of a BMC over RMCP (IPMI v1.5):
.PP
.RS
pyipmi \-I rmcp \-H 10.0.0.1 \-U admin \-P admin sdr list
.RE
.PP
Print the FRU of the local BMC using the Linux IPMI driver:
.PP
.RS
pyipmi \-I ipmidev fru print
.RE

[SEE ALSO]
.BR ipmitool (1)
